{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/713613-compact-the-red-envelope-society","id":713613,"title":"[Compact] The Red Envelope Society","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-21T20:44:20-07:00","id":713613,"title":"[Compact] The Red Envelope Society","content":"<b>The Red Envelope Society - </b><span style=\"font-family:Lucida Sans Unicode\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u7d05\u5305\u4f1a </b></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> A birthday gift, a party favor, a token of appreciation. <i>Hongbao</i> exchange hands. <i>Guanxi</i> is cultivated. In the People's Republic these ubiquitous red envelopes typically hold money, the amount hidden from the vulgarity of public display. Sometimes though... they contain instructions. Instructions from a secretive group, bound by a code of secrecy and sacrifice, that works in the shadows against the creatures that hide there. <i>Hongbaohui</i>, the Red Envelope Society.<br /> <br /> They come from many parts of society; businessmen, cab drivers, party functionaries, construction workers. They all had brushes with the unexplained, all suffered somehow at the hands of unseen tormenters, and they kept quiet. What else were they supposed to do? At best they'd be a labeled a lunatic, at worst they could be named a bad element or a class enemy. Silence was survival. Somehow though, there were people who knew. The first red envelope came anonymously, buried in a stack of identical well-wishes or slipped under their door, offering them help.<br /> <br /> Help can come in many different forms. Money, a train ticket, the keys to a locker, sometimes just an address and a name. One never knows who is going to hand them an envelope, and as a rule they do not ask many questions. Circles of acquaintances exist within the society, but rarely do they discuss it out loud and rarely does one individual know more than a handful of other members. As such, whispers abound as to its true origin and purpose.<br /> <br /> Some say the society has existed for centuries, beginning in the occult intrigues of the Tang and handed down through the scholar-gentry. Others believe it to be a mystical association formed during the tumultuous Qing, drawing its initiates from criminals and would-be reformers. Many link the society to the Cultural Revolution and an eccentric cohort of red guards, taking the struggle against feudalism to its incarnate superstitions. The truth may indeed be a combination of these, or something altogether stranger. Dark rumors persist that the red envelopes are printed somewhere deep in the apparatus of the party, that their instructions are merely cogs in a still grander and more insidious machine. What is known, and what matters to the society's clandestine members, is that they are protecting people. Lives are saved, loss is avenged, and monsters are dragged from the shadows.<br /> <br /> ______<br /> <br /> Status 0 \u2013 You've received your first envelope and followed its instructions to the bitter end. Your benefactors are mysterious but the advice they've given you has continued to come in handy. You gain a free specialization in your choice of either Streetwise or Politics.<br /> <br /> Status 00 \u2013 You've met one of the envelope couriers face to face and are trusted enough to be introduced to other members. Your own vendetta has been satisfied and now you've begun paying forward your debt to the society. You gain a dot of Allies (Red Envelope Society).<br /> <br /> Status 000 \u2013 You've been enlisted as a handler for the society, embedded ever deeper in the hidden world it inhabits. The interlocking movements of the society's agenda and the plots it grapples are becoming clearer to you. You gain either the Fixer merit or the Small Unit Tactics merit.<br /> <br /> Status 0000 \u2013 You're in too far to back out now. The connections are everywhere; haunted buildings, mind controlled officials, earthquake patterns along important ley lines. As soon as you think you've gained some clarity the answer seems to slip away. You gain the merit Omen Sensitivity.<br /> <br /> Status 00000 \u2013 You've become one of the society's operators, a backroom ghost and bureaucratic aberration. You are the originator of many red envelopes, but still you receive instructions of your own. You gain three dots of Anonymity as attempts to quantify you become lost in the murk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2507,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","user":"Caitiff Primogen","date":". 10-21-2015, 11:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}